      "title": "Public service union refuses to back Labor at Victorian election, condemning job cuts and $1.2bn consultant spend",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/cpsu-public-servants-union-refuses-to-back-labor-at-victorian-election",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive: </strong>Community and Public Sector Union denounces ‘privatisation by stealth’, joining growing number of unions turning on Carroll government</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Victoria’s public servants union says it will not support Labor at this month’s state election, condemning the government for cutting public service jobs while spending $1.2bn on consultants.</p><p>The Community and Public Sector Union (CPSU) will announce the decision on Wednesday, <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/31/more-unions-down-tools-in-labors-victorian-election-campaign-as-trust-broken\">joining several other unions</a> that have refused to back Labor or are actively campaigning against the government ahead of the 28 November poll.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/cpsu-public-servants-union-refuses-to-back-labor-at-victorian-election\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T14:00:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Snowy Hydro 2.0 executives awarded bonuses totalling $751,925 despite cost blowout",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/snowy-hydro-20-executives-awarded-bonuses-totalling-751925-despite-cost-blowout",
      "description": "<p>Annual reports show NSW renewable company’s CEO opted out of cash bonus, while CSIRO’s chief received an extra $200,000</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Executives at the troubled <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/oct/03/snowy-hydro-20-flags-another-cost-blowout-with-12bn-price-tag-now-considered-unachievable\">Snowy Hydro </a>company collectively banked bonuses worth a combined $751,925 in the last financial year, despite its renewable energy project blowing out to 12 times its original cost.</p><p>But Guardian Australia can reveal chief executive, Dennis Barnes, who has a base salary of $1,845,126, opted not to accept the extra cash.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/snowy-hydro-20-executives-awarded-bonuses-totalling-751925-despite-cost-blowout\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T14:00:44"
    },
